--    "content": "# [Informational] REST API Architecture and OpenAPI Integration Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nSoftware projects that attempt to manually maintain hundreds of static wiki pages for every REST endpoint inevitably suffer from documentation drift: code changes, parameters evolve, but static documentation falls behind, creating frustration and integration bugs.\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban adheres to the **In-Code OpenAPI Single Source of Truth** architecture:\n- All REST endpoints are declared with comprehensive Pydantic models, detailed FastAPI docstrings, summaries, response schemas, and parameter constraints directly in the Python source code (`kanban/api/v1/*.py`).\n- The canonical OpenAPI 3.1.0 specification is automatically generated by the FastAPI backend at `/api/openapi.json` and mirrored in the repository at `kanban/web/openapi.json` (`242+` paths, `316+` operations, `314+` schemas, regenerated via `python -m kanban.tools.export_openapi kanban/web/openapi.json`).\n- Interactive documentation is hosted at `/api/docs` (Swagger UI) and `/api/redoc` (ReDoc) directly from the application server with self-contained assets.\n- The web frontend generates its type-safe TypeScript API client directly from this schema (`pnpm --dir kanban/web run gen:api` producing `kanban/web/src/api/schema.gen.ts`).\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph Backend[\"FastAPI Backend Source\"]\n        Pydantic[\"Pydantic Schemas<br/>& Field Validators\"]\n        Routes[\"242+ FastAPI Routes<br/>kanban/api/v1/*.py\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph SchemaGen[\"Canonical OpenAPI Export\"]\n        OpenAPI[\"OpenAPI 3.1.0 JSON<br/>/api/openapi.json\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Frontend[\"TypeScript Client & UI\"]\n        TSGen[\"openapi-typescript<br/>pnpm run gen:api\"]\n        SDK[\"Type-Safe Client SDK<br/>src/api/schema.gen.ts\"]\n        UI[\"React 19 SPA<br/>Board, Drawer, Studios\"]\n    end\n\n    Pydantic --> Routes\n    Routes -->|Automatic Introspection| OpenAPI\n    OpenAPI -->|Code Generation| TSGen\n    TSGen --> SDK\n    SDK --> UI\n```\n\n---\n\n## Documentation and Schema Endpoints\n\nWhen running \ud83d\udc4dkanban (in standalone mode or production), developers and integrations can access:\n\n| Endpoint / File | Interface | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`/api/docs`** | Swagger UI | Interactive API explorer rendered with local CSS and zero external CDNs. |\n| **`/api/redoc`** | ReDoc | Responsive technical documentation view of all endpoints, parameters, and models. |\n| **`/api/openapi.json`** | Raw OpenAPI 3.1.0 JSON | Machine-readable FastAPI schema (`242+` paths, `316+` operations, `314+` schemas). |\n| **`kanban/web/openapi.json`** | In-Repo JSON Snapshot | Version-controlled OpenAPI specification checked by CI (`pnpm run check:api`). |\n| **`kanban/web/src/api/schema.gen.ts`** | Generated TypeScript SDK | Strictly typed interfaces, request parameters, and response schemas. |\n| **`kanban/api/v1/*.py`** | In-Code Python Source | Authoritative FastAPI route docstrings, summaries, tags, and Pydantic `Field` docs. |\n\n---\n\n## REST API Architectural Principles\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Client as Client / Agent\n    participant FastAPI as FastAPI Router\n    participant Auth as Auth & AAL2 Dependency\n    participant DB as PostgreSQL (FORCE RLS)\n    participant San as Markdown Sanitizer\n\n    Client->>FastAPI: HTTP PATCH /api/v1/issues/{id} (If-Match: ETag)\n    FastAPI->>Auth: Validate Session / Token & AAL2 Level\n    alt Invalid Auth or Missing AAL2\n        Auth-->>Client: 401 Unauthorized / 403 Forbidden (RFC 7807)\n    else Authenticated\n        Auth->>DB: BEGIN TX & SET LOCAL app.current_principal_id = :id\n        FastAPI->>DB: Check ETag & Select Row with RLS\n        alt ETag Mismatch (Lost Update Detected)\n            FastAPI-->>Client: 412 Precondition Failed\n        else ETag Matched\n            FastAPI->>San: Sanitize Hostile Unicode & HTML\n            San-->>FastAPI: Clean Canonical Markdown\n            FastAPI->>DB: UPDATE issue & Append Activity Ledger\n            DB-->>FastAPI: Commit TX\n            FastAPI-->>Client: 200 OK (New ETag, Sanitized Payload)\n        end\n    end\n```\n\nEvery REST endpoint in \ud83d\udc4dkanban adheres to strict architectural invariants:\n\n### 1. Consistent RFC 7807 Error Responses\nAll error responses return structured RFC 7807 Problem Details JSON:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"https://kanban.hackedyour.info/errors/LOCKOUT_PREVENTED\",\n  \"title\": \"Lockout Prevented\",\n  \"status\": 409,\n  \"detail\": \"Cannot disable the sole remaining active admin authentication card.\",\n  \"instance\": \"/api/v1/admin/auth/cards/01932e6b-7341-789a-bc01-123456789abc\",\n  \"code\": \"LOCKOUT_PREVENTED\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-15T23:50:00Z\"\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Multi-Factor Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (AAL2)\nEvery route under `/api/v1/admin/*` enforces multi-factor verification at the FastAPI dependency layer:\n\n```python\n@router.post(\n    \"/admin/auth/cards/{card_id}/reorder\",\n    dependencies=[Depends(require_admin_aal2)],\n    summary=\"Reorder Authentication Cards\",\n    description=\"Updates sort rank of an authentication card. Enforces AAL2 admin session.\"\n)\nasync def reorder_auth_card(...): ...\n```\nAPI tests enforce this contract via `assert_admin_routes_protected`, rejecting any PR that adds an admin endpoint without the required `require_admin_aal2` dependency.\n\n### 3. Concurrency Protection with ETag and `If-Match`\nTo prevent the lost-update problem when multiple engineers or AI agents edit tickets simultaneously:\n- Read endpoints return an `ETag` header containing a SHA-256 hash of the object version.\n- Mutation endpoints (`PATCH /api/v1/issues/{id}`, `PUT /api/v1/docs/{id}`) accept an `If-Match` header.\n- If the current database record version differs from the provided `If-Match` header, the request is rejected with `412 Precondition Failed`.\n\n### 4. Zero-Context Fail-Closed Database Isolation\nREST route handlers do not query PostgreSQL as a superuser. Each request handler binds the authenticated principal ID to the session context (`SET LOCAL app.current_principal_id = :id`) within an explicit database transaction. If authentication is absent, PostgreSQL Row-Level Security policies evaluate to false and return zero records.\n\n---\n\n## Route Module Organization\n\nThe 242+ REST API endpoints (316+ operations across 314+ schemas) are organized into cohesive domain modules under `kanban/api/v1/`:\n\n```\nkanban/api/v1/\n|-- auth_*.py           # Multi-card authentication (local, ldap, oidc, session, setup, webauthn, mfa)\n|-- workspaces.py       # Workspace provisioning, member invitations, theme configuration\n|-- projects.py         # Project lifecycle, custom state configuration, member bindings\n|-- issues.py           # Work items, quick-create, property updates, sub-tasks, comments\n|-- issue_*.py          # Issue operations (archive, copy, delete, move, provenance, trees, workflow)\n|-- cycles.py           # Sprint cycles, rollover automation, velocity calculations\n|-- modules.py          # Functional modules, completion tracking, feature grouping\n|-- docs.py             # Hierarchical technical documentation, ltree traversal, version diffs\n|-- stickies.py         # Digital sticky notes, color categorization, smart promotion\n|-- custom_fields*.py   # Custom scripted fields, approvals, Wasmtime/nsjail execution\n|-- transitions.py      # Workflow transitions, helper engine execution, gate evaluation\n|-- search.py           # Hybrid lexical and semantic search endpoints\n|-- media_proxy.py      # Cookieless, HMAC-signed external image proxy (GET /api/v1/media-proxy)\n|-- oauth.py            # OAuth 2.0 / OIDC provider endpoints, PKCE, device code authorization\n|-- repo_bindings.py    # Remote git repository bindings and runner pools\n|-- agent_definitions.py# Agent definition catalog and validation\n|-- admin/              # Admin-only AAL2 governance modules\n|   |-- auth_cards.py   # Multi-card auth administration\n|   |-- destructive.py  # Blast-radius calculations and 2-stage confirmations\n|   |-- link_auditor.py # Universal Object Graph link audits and repair\n|   `-- workspace_settings.py # Workspace configuration and security parameters\n`-- system*.py          # Platform summary, status, licensing, and CycloneDX 1.5 SBOM\n```\n\n---\n\n## Generating Client SDKs and Syncing Schemas\n\nTo update the frontend TypeScript client after modifying backend FastAPI route signatures:\n\n```bash\n# Step 1: Export latest OpenAPI JSON from the FastAPI application\npython -m kanban.tools.export_openapi kanban/web/openapi.json\n\n# Step 2: Regenerate the TypeScript SDK types\npnpm --dir kanban/web run gen:api\n\n# Step 3: Verify TypeScript compilation\npnpm --dir kanban/web run build\n```\n\nThis automated synchronization ensures that frontend UI components, test runners, and backend routes stay in lockstep with zero documentation lag.\n\n---\n\n## Administrative API and MCP Key Surfaces\n\nThe administrative REST API operates alongside the Model Context Protocol (MCP) server, offering fine-grained permission scoping, token rotation, and runtime health diagnostics.\n\n![MCP Access Studio and Scoped Token Management](images/13-mcp-access-studio.png)\n\n![System Settings and API Diagnostics](images/26-system-settings.png)\n"
