Unix domain socket (`/var/run/postgresql/.s.PGSQL.5432`). TCP networking for PostgreSQL is disabled (`listen_addresses = ''`), preventing network-level database intrusion.\n- **Volume Persistence Probe:** On startup, the container verifies that `/var/lib/kanban/data` is mounted to a persistent volume. If an ephemeral container filesystem is detected, the UI displays a dismissible amber warning banner alerting the operator to attach persistent storage before creating production data.\n- **Status and Health Panel:** Accessible at `/admin/standalone`, this panel reports database uptime, socket latency, storage utilization, and single-click export to multi-container Compose bundles.\n\n![Standalone Status Panel](images/04-standalone-status-panel.png)\n\n### Workspace Home and Initial State\n\nOnce the container finishes initialization, users land on the clean, breathable Workspace Home. The workspace view provides instant access to projects, work items, stickies, and system configuration.\n\n![Workspace Home](images/05-workspace-home.png)\n\n---\n\n## Multi-Container Production Architecture (`docker compose`)\n\nFor production environments, \ud83d\udc4dkanban deploys as a multi-container stack compartmentalized across five isolated Docker networks.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Proxy[\"Reverse Proxy (Caddy / Nginx)\"] -->|edge_net: 8921| App[\"\ud83d\udc4dkanban App Container (FastAPI)<br/>- Uvicorn ASGI workers (UID 65532)<br/>- Multi-Card Auth & AAL2 Middleware<br/>- WebSocket Hub & Markdown Pipelines\"]\n    Runners[\"Distributed Agent Runners\"] -->|mTLS: 8444| App\n    \n    App -->|data_net: 5432| PG[\"PostgreSQL 16 DB<br/>- FORCE RLS (100%)<br/>- pgvector + ltree<br/>- Isolated data_net\"]\n    App -->|sandbox_net: IPC| Sandbox[\"Sandbox Execution Runtime<br/>- Wasmtime runtime<br/>- nsjail runner<br/>- Zero data_net route\"]\n    App -->|egress_llm_net: 443| AI[\"External AI Providers<br/>- OpenAI, Gemini<br/>- Local Ollama\"]\n    App -.->|internal_net| InternalMCP[\"Private /internal/v1/mcp/*<br/>- Runner task dispatch<br/>- Zero edge routing\"]\n```\n\n![Standalone to Production Compose Export](images/27-standalone-compose-export.png)\n\n![System Settings and Production Diagnostics](images/26-system-settings.png)\n\n### The 5-Network Isolation Matrix\n\nTo prevent lateral movement and enforce zero-trust network boundaries, container communication is segregated into five distinct networks:\n\n| Network Name | Connected Services | Allowed Ingress / Egress | Security Rationale |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`edge_net`** | Reverse proxy, Web application | External HTTP/S (8921) & Runner mTLS (8444) | Shields backend application from direct exposure; terminates TLS and dedicated mTLS. Blocks external `/internal/v1/mcp/*`. |\n| **`app_net`** | Web application, Redis / cache (optional) | Inter-service caching, session distribution, internal MCP | Segregates application control plane; isolates `/internal/v1/mcp/*` routes from external edge ingress. |\n| **`data_net`** | Web application, PostgreSQL 16 | PostgreSQL TCP (port 5432) | Strictly internal. The database has zero external routing or internet gateway. |\n| **`sandbox_net`** | Web application, Custom Script runner | Unix socket / IPC pipe | Completely air-gapped. Scripts have zero route to `data_net` or the internet. |\n| **`egress_llm_net`** | Web application, LLM egress gateway | Outbound HTTPS to pinned AI API endpoints | Limits external outbound traffic exclusively to configured LLM APIs. |\n\n### Monotonic CredentialBoundary Across Container Mesh\n\nAcross all service boundaries in the multi-container topology, security tokens enforce monotonic `CredentialBoundary` constraints:\n- **Capability Bitmask Ceiling:** Tokens cannot exceed the active permissions of the issuing principal. A key minted with `capability_mask = 1` (`VIEW` only) emits strictly `${surface}:read` scopes and cannot perform mutating operations across any network boundary.\n- **CIDR Subnet Pinning:** Invocations carry optional `allowed_cidrs` constraints, rejecting requests originating from non-whitelisted IP addresses before requests reach application or database layers.\n\n### Process Hardening and Least Privilege\n\nEvery container in the production stack enforces strict Linux security controls:\n- **Non-Root Execution:** Runs under dedicated unprivileged system users (`UID 65532`, `GID 65532`).\n- **Capability Dropping:** Drops all Linux capabilities on initialization (`--cap-drop=ALL`).\n- **No New Privileges:** Enforces `setpriv --no-new-privs` to prevent setuid privilege escalation.\n- **Read-Only Root Filesystem:** Container root filesystems are mounted read-only (`read_only: true`), with writable space restricted to tmpfs mounts for `/tmp` and `/run`.\n\n---\n\n## Supply Chain Integrity and Permissive Licensing\n\nIn strict accordance with enterprise governance requirements:\n- **Pure Apache-2.0:** All platform source code, libraries, and build targets are licensed under Apache-2.0.\n- **Zero Viral Licenses:** The dependency tree is continuously audited in CI to reject any runtime dependencies with copyleft licenses (GPL, AGPL, LGPL, SSPL).\n- **Pinned Dependencies:** All Python dependencies (`pyproject.toml`) and JavaScript packages (`package.json`) are cryptographically locked with exact hashes.\n"
